💭 Compresses one file, so that a decompressor that is not ours can be asked what it
💭 makes of the stream. It imports the package as any program would: what gzip reads is
💭 what the built package wrote. Built into build/bin/deflate-tool.
💭
💭   deflate-tool hex <file>      the stream, as hex digits on one line
💭   deflate-tool quiet <file>    nothing: for seeing how long it takes
💭
💭 The stream goes out as text because the stock files package can only write a file
💭 through a call that raises and returns nothing, and handling such a call takes a 🆗
💭 that binds no value, which this compiler gets wrong. A script turns the digits back.
